  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)=x{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}+y.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\u2207f$ is conservative\n- ${\\int }_{C}\u2207f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- ${\u222e}_{C}\u2207f\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$",
  "worked_solution": "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $\u0393=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\n\u0393={\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The vector field $\u2207f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement II is false. The result $\u0393=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\n- Statement III is false. The circulation $\u0393=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
